window.IDP_ATLAS_POEMS=[{"order":1,"slug":"broken","title":"Broken","excerpt":"You look at this world with hatred, Anger burns in your heart, All the things that have been said, Are tearing your life apart. Sadness overwhelms you, You cry all day and night, The stuff you tr…","text":"You look at this world with hatred, Anger burns in your heart, All the things that have been said, Are tearing your life apart. Sadness overwhelms you, You cry all day and night, The stuff you try to do, Makes you wonder: is life worth the fight? I come to you and write this, In hopes that you will see, That you can't just be faithless, That life is what you make it to be. I know that things seem bad, But you WILL get through the days, They're exactly like a fad: They're bound to go away. On days you feel you can't go on, And you've done all you think you can do, Please just remember this poem, And know I'll be there for you."},{"order":2,"slug":"missing","title":"Missing You","excerpt":"When we are apart, My heart is torn open, But right from the start, You left my heart broken. Somehow I still love you, As I always will, But words just won't do, You need to see that it's real.…","text":"When we are apart, My heart is torn open, But right from the start, You left my heart broken. Somehow I still love you, As I always will, But words just won't do, You need to see that it's real. I wish somehow I could convey, How you make me feel, How I think of you every day, And how I love you still. It's very hard at most, When I don't know what you think, Just when I feel we're getting close, I screw up and your feelings sink. I say in advance, That I'm sorry for what I'll do, So I take you by the hands, And ask, \"Do you love me too?\""},{"order":3,"slug":"dream","title":"Dream","excerpt":"Laying on the beach, On a cool summer's night, You within my reach, Bathed in pale moonlight. All at once we're taken, Lifted high above the clouds, I look and try to make them, Take us to the gr…","text":"Laying on the beach, On a cool summer's night, You within my reach, Bathed in pale moonlight. All at once we're taken, Lifted high above the clouds, I look and try to make them, Take us to the ground. Far below I can see, Lights within the waves, And the person holding me, Says, \"We couldn't be saved.\" Below in the water floating, Two objects drifting a sea, And I realize with heart beating, The objects are you and me. Looking up I spied, The gates of heaven's door, And realized that we died, To live in heaven forevermore."},{"order":4,"slug":"totheone","title":"To the One I Love","excerpt":"To the one I love, The one that I adore, My only goal in life, The one that I live for: Even though we fight, More than we get along, I hope our relationship, Will never go wrong. I love to be wi…","text":"To the one I love, The one that I adore, My only goal in life, The one that I live for: Even though we fight, More than we get along, I hope our relationship, Will never go wrong. I love to be with you, I love when you're around; I'm so glad I'm the one, That you just now found. Though you may not see, Just what you mean to me, My love for you forever, And ever will always be. I know you love me, And I know that you care; That is why I treasure, The love that we share. I want you to know, That I am here for you, Whatever is going on, I will help you through. To the one I love, The one that I adore: With each passing day, I love you more and more."},{"order":5,"slug":"time","title":"Time","excerpt":"Days slipping away, Just out of our grasp, There goes another day, Gone into the past. It doesn’t seem to last, At all very long, So while these moments pass, Let’s try to hold on. The minutes sl…","text":"Days slipping away, Just out of our grasp, There goes another day, Gone into the past. It doesn’t seem to last, At all very long, So while these moments pass, Let’s try to hold on. The minutes slip by us, Faster and faster still, The seconds they deny us, Are against our will. So lets hold on to these moments, Forever as long as can be, Now put down your defense, And let yourself be free. Let’s make these good times last, Be together, happy at least, Before they’re gone into the past, Just out of our reach."},{"order":6,"slug":"uncertain","title":"Uncertain","excerpt":"Day after day I try, To be as nice as I can, To hold back the tears as I cry, And show that I'm a man. I want to be your friend, To be there for you always, To have it never end, To last for the…","text":"Day after day I try, To be as nice as I can, To hold back the tears as I cry, And show that I'm a man. I want to be your friend, To be there for you always, To have it never end, To last for the rest of the days. But nothing seems to work, All you do is reject me, Am I being a jerk? Or are you playing \"hard to get me?\" You hide behind your laughter, But tears fall at night in your bed, What do you think I'm after? I wish I knew what went on in your head... All I want is to help you, To protect you and to defend, But in order for me to love you, You have to let me in. Actions speak louder than words, And your actions say you hate me, I know that it seems absurd, But I've liked you more lately."},{"order":7,"slug":"youtoknow","title":"I Want You to Know","excerpt":"I want you to know, Just a few things, The hate that you've caused, And the sadness it brings. I want you to know, What you've done to me, How it tears me apart, And makes me lonely. I want you t…","text":"I want you to know, Just a few things, The hate that you've caused, And the sadness it brings. I want you to know, What you've done to me, How it tears me apart, And makes me lonely. I want you to know, How sad that I've been, How hopeless you seem, And how you won't let me in. I want you to know, How difficult you are, Every time that I leave, I don't get very far. I want you to know, There's something about you, Something that tells me, I can't live without you. I want you to know, How much I want to help, How everything's for you, And nothing's for myself. I want you to know, I think of you daily, Though you tick me off, I love you anyway. I want you to know, That I'm completely sincere, No matter what it is, I will always be here."},{"order":8,"slug":"gone","title":"Gone","excerpt":"My love for you burns like a fire, I need the heat and I want to be near, When I'm with you I feel ten times higher, But things have changed I fear. Gone are the days I longed to be, Within your…","text":"My love for you burns like a fire, I need the heat and I want to be near, When I'm with you I feel ten times higher, But things have changed I fear. Gone are the days I longed to be, Within your marvelous presence, Scrambling to try so earnestly, To see you again every chance. I now am filled with deep remorse, For my love was taken in vain, Like racing through the driving course, Learning you're in the wrong lane. For so long you were the object of my affection, The one I thought of daily and nightly too, I realized what was wrong and made the correction, Finally realized that I'm not meant for you. You lie and steal from poor fools like me, Stupid enough to foolishly give their love away, I want you to know I will no longer be, Stupid enough to love you one more day."},{"order":9,"slug":"lovehim","title":"You Love Him","excerpt":"I see from across the room, In his direction you stare, Silently I wonder, Why it's him for whom you care. Your every breath, your every thought, Consumed with visions of him, Every course of act…","text":"I see from across the room, In his direction you stare, Silently I wonder, Why it's him for whom you care. Your every breath, your every thought, Consumed with visions of him, Every course of action, every move you make, Based on lusts and whims. It seems like to me, You want what you can't have, Take for granted what you do, And just shake it off and laugh. If you neglect your true friends, On the gamble of just one person, You'll have no one there to help, And your problems will only worsen. But liking him is your choice, I cannot change your mind, I am but just one small voice, Who is trying to be kind. So with tears streaming down my face, I will let you leave, Just remember when everyone's gone, You'll still always have me."},{"order":10,"slug":"life","title":"Life","excerpt":"In life I've found out lots, And as near as I can tell, You have to take the shots, And things aren't always well. No matter where you turn, Some things are hard to see, One thing that I've learn…","text":"In life I've found out lots, And as near as I can tell, You have to take the shots, And things aren't always well. No matter where you turn, Some things are hard to see, One thing that I've learned, Hatred only brings misery. What's the point of trying? When you've got nothing to gain, I know as I sit here crying, Only people who love feel pain. When everyone around, Tells you what you do, Sometimes you wonder aloud, Maybe what they say is true. Seems the worst pain's left unspoken, Silently coming up behind, When all love is made to be broken, And nothing's what it is in the light."},{"order":11,"slug":"thepoint","title":"What's the Point?","excerpt":"What's the point of trying, When all you do is wrong? What's the point of crying, When no one hears your song? What's the point of love, When nothing goes your way? What's the point of effort, Wh…","text":"What's the point of trying, When all you do is wrong? What's the point of crying, When no one hears your song? What's the point of love, When nothing goes your way? What's the point of effort, When you can't take another day? What's the point of memories? They all will fade away, What's the point of sensitivity? You'll just get called gay... What's the point of happiness? It lasts only a short time, What's the point of sadness? It just ruins your life. What's the point of seeing? When everything's a lie? What's the point of believing? When all you ask is why? What's the point of life? Filled with pain and strife, And what's the point of me? Filled with sadness and misery."},{"order":12,"slug":"panic","title":"Panic","excerpt":"At night when I'm alone, And lying in my bed, Things talk to me, They live inside my head. I don't know what they say, But I'm overcome with fear, I keep trying to ignore it, Hoping it will disap…","text":"At night when I'm alone, And lying in my bed, Things talk to me, They live inside my head. I don't know what they say, But I'm overcome with fear, I keep trying to ignore it, Hoping it will disappear. I sit there and I pray, For God to bring me peace, To take away the fear, And to please just let me sleep. So I lay there still, Waiting for sleep to come, Praying for tomorrow, For this night to be done."},{"order":13,"slug":"fiftythings","title":"Fifty Things I Love About You","excerpt":"From your beautiful hair, To your petite little hands, To the clothes that you wear, To the way that you dance, Your cute little nose, The way you're so sweet, The beauty that goes, From your hea…","text":"From your beautiful hair, To your petite little hands, To the clothes that you wear, To the way that you dance, Your cute little nose, The way you're so sweet, The beauty that goes, From your head to your feet, The way that you smell, That's so very lovely, The way I can tell, That you really love me, How you call every day, The conversations we have, The funny things you say, The way you make me laugh, How you say you'll \"get me,\" How your love is so rare, How you always say you miss me, And wish that I was there, The beating of your heart, As we lay close together, How I wish we wouldn't part, And could stay like this forever, From the things that you're into, To the way that you're nice, How I want to be with you, The rest of my life, How I never doubt you, When you make me wait, The little things about you, That I love to hate, Your wonderful smile, Your beautiful eyes, How I waited a while, To see your surprise, How you love God, And are not afraid to show it, How you love me lots, And how you let me know it, The way that you're so kind, Sweet, beautiful, and loving, How you're always on my mind, And without you I am nothing, The way you're always cold, The way I know you must be, And when your hand I hold, How I remember that I'm lucky, How you love me so, And never want to leave me, How you don't want me to go, And every chance you see me, How I wish I could be there, How I think of you every night, How I would hold you when you're scared, And tell you everything's all right, The way there is so much about you, Too much for me to name, I don't know what I'd do without you, I'd never be the same. These are the things I love, From your personality to your looks, And fifty's not enough, I could write enough to fill fifteen books, Every reason I listed is true, I must be your biggest fan, But the greatest thing about you, Is how you love me for who I am."},{"order":14,"slug":"loveyoumore","title":"I Love You More","excerpt":"I love you more than life itself, For life in itself is worthless, Without someone with which to share, The beauty of life's purpose. I love you more than you can know, You've helped more than yo…","text":"I love you more than life itself, For life in itself is worthless, Without someone with which to share, The beauty of life's purpose. I love you more than you can know, You've helped more than you can imagine, I once was lonely, now I see, And realize miracles still happen. I love you more for who you are, Than what you can or will be, Whenever I am feeling empty, You come along and fill me. I love you more than happiness, For my happiness comes from you, For so long I waited for someone, And now my wish has come true. I love you more with each passing day, More than anyone before, But no matter how much you love me, I will always love you more."},{"order":15,"slug":"confusion","title":"Confusion","excerpt":"I've been searching, For someone lovely, All I want, Is someone who loves me. Someone who cares, If I'm happy or not, And when I screw up, Whose love will not stop. You make it all better, All ba…","text":"I've been searching, For someone lovely, All I want, Is someone who loves me. Someone who cares, If I'm happy or not, And when I screw up, Whose love will not stop. You make it all better, All bad things go away, You help me so much, And give strength for another day. I love you so much, I hope we make it through, You can make me smile, Something few people can do. You mend all that's broken, Pull together the pieces, You give me reason to live, And the strength to release it. I want to make you happy, Somehow I wish to repay, I want to be with you forever, And try the rest of my days. I know I really love you, But you're too good to be true, And I know that it sounds crazy, But I'm afraid of losing you. I love you, but... I feel I love too much, I know you love me, but... It doesn't seem like it's enough. I think I love you too much, Even though it's what you deserve, But loving you too much, I'm sure, just gets on your nerves. I don't like one-sided love, In a way it makes me feel used, Understand that I'm not mad, I'm just a bit confused. Of course I love you more, But I need to be loved back, It sounds like you don't love me, But I know you can't mean that. So I will come down to your level, And make both our loves equal, So that they may grow together, And in that be more meaningful. You yourself are the one, I'm always thinking of, But I'm still afraid of losing, The only one I love."},{"order":16,"slug":"descent","title":"The Descent of Happiness","excerpt":"There! I can see it! Love within my grasp! I reach for it, it slips away, I knew it wouldn't last. Now life is slipping away, Smashed up all my dreams, Breaking down and broken, Dying more each d…","text":"There! I can see it! Love within my grasp! I reach for it, it slips away, I knew it wouldn't last. Now life is slipping away, Smashed up all my dreams, Breaking down and broken, Dying more each day it seems. I was at first so happy, Now everything has fallen apart, Tearing open my insides, And ripping out my heart. In this flailing madness, What I once loved now despised, Cowering at the sight of you, Covering my eyes. In this bitter victory, I feel like love I have won, And as I look back at the battle, I see my goal, my love, is gone."},{"order":17,"slug":"reason","title":"The Reason","excerpt":"All my life I have searched, For one person to truly care, Someone I can always talk to, Someone who is always there. Someone who won't let me down, And if they do will bring me back up, One who…","text":"All my life I have searched, For one person to truly care, Someone I can always talk to, Someone who is always there. Someone who won't let me down, And if they do will bring me back up, One who makes me happy inside, At the slightest sensation of touch. I've looked and tried with many, But all I could find was hurt, And now I want you to know, I want us to please make this work. I've wondered if life was worth living, And now I can say that's true, For all of the things that you've done, I want you to know I love you."},{"order":18,"slug":"belike","title":"What Would It Be Like?","excerpt":"What would life be like, If we had never met? Where would we both be, If there was nothing to forget? How would my life be, If we never got together? Would I still be happy, Or would I stay depre…","text":"What would life be like, If we had never met? Where would we both be, If there was nothing to forget? How would my life be, If we never got together? Would I still be happy, Or would I stay depressed forever? What would you be doing, If we had never talked? If I hadn't e-mailed you, Would it be my fault? How would I be different, If I had never met you? Would I be better or worse, Or would I ever get through? I think it's amazing, How one action can cause so much, How it changes your life, It almost seems like luck. But like you say so often, It's all part of God's plan, And I think now more than ever, That I truly understand."},{"order":19,"slug":"sometimes","title":"Sometimes","excerpt":"Sometimes I feel as if I'm falling, And can never come back again, And that no matter how hard I'm trying, I'll never be able to win. I feel as if there's nothing left, Every corner now explored,…","text":"Sometimes I feel as if I'm falling, And can never come back again, And that no matter how hard I'm trying, I'll never be able to win. I feel as if there's nothing left, Every corner now explored, There's nothing to look forward to, Nothing good is left in store. Sometimes I wish that I could be, A better person than I am, That I could be a better Christian, That I could be a better friend. Sometimes I am so happy, That I don't think I can stand it, And other times I get so mad, It feels like someone planned it. Sometimes I drift and wander, And wonder why that I'm alive, What I'm supposed to do, And wonder what's the point of life. Sometimes I feel worthless, But I know it can't be true, If I was you wouldn't love me, But luckily you do."},{"order":20,"slug":"dontyou","title":"Don't You?","excerpt":"You love me, don't you? Then why can't you show it? If you really did, Wouldn't you let me know it? You love me, don't you? Then why don't we do things? If you're tired of movies, Then I'm sure w…","text":"You love me, don't you? Then why can't you show it? If you really did, Wouldn't you let me know it? You love me, don't you? Then why don't we do things? If you're tired of movies, Then I'm sure we'll find new things. You love me, don't you? Then why can't you tell me? Just tell me the words, So I know that you really. You love me, don't you? Then how am I not the one? Instead of getting most your love, I receive next to none. Maybe I am selfish, Or want more than I deserve, Maybe I'm impatient, But then maybe I will learn. That you do love me, I just need to wait, Your love will eventually catch up, Just at a slower rate."},{"order":21,"slug":"lovedream","title":"The Love Dream","excerpt":"In a dream, I am our love, Dangling from the edge of repair, High, high above the ground, Above the pit of despair. Clawing and grabbing, I'm losing my grip, My fingers start aching, They're star…","text":"In a dream, I am our love, Dangling from the edge of repair, High, high above the ground, Above the pit of despair. Clawing and grabbing, I'm losing my grip, My fingers start aching, They're starting to slip. I look down below, Gauging the distance, In my mind I know, That I must resist it. But you can't resist it, After all, it's gravity, Nothing I can do to save it, From this tragedy. It really gets me down, To know that there's no way, So I let go of the ledge, And just accept my fate.."},{"order":22,"slug":"fragile","title":"Fragile","excerpt":"Have you ever held a glass, And felt its fragility? Or watched a deer running, And marveled at it's agility? Or looked at the world around, And seen how quickly it would fall, If the thing that h…","text":"Have you ever held a glass, And felt its fragility? Or watched a deer running, And marveled at it's agility? Or looked at the world around, And seen how quickly it would fall, If the thing that held it up was gone, And then you lost it all? My life is like the glass, It's fragile, and does not bend, With the only constant in relationships, Is that eventually they'll end. You are like the table, Supporting and standing tall, Keeping me from plunging down, Holding me up, preventing the fall. The Table is taken from the glass, The ground rushing quickly near, Falling quickly and silently, Like the agile deer. No way to escape gravity, With a smash, pieces fly through the room, The sound of my world crashing down, Knowing my dreams will be gone soon. So as I lay in pieces, I pray I get put back together, That someone will come be my glue, And keep me together forever."},{"order":23,"slug":"deception","title":"Deception","excerpt":"The lies flow like water, The hate pours out like rain, Fear and confusion settle in, Joy's been all but slain. Lured me into your web, Baited me into your trap, Disoriented and confused, Like be…","text":"The lies flow like water, The hate pours out like rain, Fear and confusion settle in, Joy's been all but slain. Lured me into your web, Baited me into your trap, Disoriented and confused, Like being lost without a map. I see you walking by, Your face that I despise, I'd rather be beaten with the truth, Than tortured by your lies. The things you couldn't tell me, Were the things I always knew, And even though you said they weren't, I knew that they were true. Now it's in the past, And you probably forgot, But I will never let it go, I've come too far to stop. One day you will pay, For all the pain that you've caused, Right now you may think that you've won, But you haven't; you have lost."},{"order":24,"slug":"theend","title":"The End","excerpt":"I soar on wings, of broken dreams, And heed the facts as mere warnings, And hurt the ones who love me most, Then wonder why I can't get close. I see the beauty in your eyes, And silently I wonder…","text":"I soar on wings, of broken dreams, And heed the facts as mere warnings, And hurt the ones who love me most, Then wonder why I can't get close. I see the beauty in your eyes, And silently I wonder why, We can't get closer than we are, Why gradually we drift apart. I loved you more than words could say, And could not go a single day, Without the beauty of your voice, Echoing with words of choice. I longed to have you here with me, To have you near, so you could see, How much I loved, how much I cared, How love that deep was truly rare. How much I longed for happiness, Compared to mine, yours was less, And even though I was worthless, My love for you I did confess. The world around, comes crashing down, I cannot reach; I'm tied and bound, And if you loved me, you would care, And rescue me from this despair, And save me from my mind's worst fears, And dam the river of my tears, And make some effort just to help, Before I snap and hurt myself. Before I snap, and hurt the ones, Who loved me first, and not for fun, Who love me when, I'm sick and ill, And though I hurt them, love me still. And though I always screw things up, They'll always come to lift me up, They'll always love me, and they'll care, When life is rough and is not fair. When girls like you, take my heart, And rip and smash and tear it apart, And walk me through, a living hell, Where nothing's good, and nothing's well. Where I remind, myself how bad, That things can get, when I am sad, I always seem, to end up hurt, And then somehow, end up a jerk. I don't see how, that could be true, When all I wanted, was for you, To tell me that, you loved me too, So I know what I must do. I am breaking up with you, And breaking my whole life in two, And even though I don't want to, It is something that I must do. Don't come around, and please don't call, Don't even bother me at all, Don't tell me that you're sad today, You were going to anyway."},{"order":25,"slug":"perfect","title":"Perfect","excerpt":"Last night, I dreamt of perfection, Everything was perfect between us, We were how we used to be, It was perfect, you should have seen us. I was happy, you were happy, We loved each other so much…","text":"Last night, I dreamt of perfection, Everything was perfect between us, We were how we used to be, It was perfect, you should have seen us. I was happy, you were happy, We loved each other so much, I fought to stay asleep, To live the dream, but had no luck. I dreamed of the perfect world, The perfect place, the perfect scene, The place that I would stay forever, If the place was not a dream. And even though it is not real, At least I could escape, At least I could forget the past, At least forget my hate. My mind is filled with memories, Which are all that I have left, And I'd use the keys of happiness, If I knew where they were kept. But things are never well for me, I guess it's just my fate, It's dreams like this, that make me wish, I'd sleep and never wake."},{"order":26,"slug":"badthoughts","title":"Bad Thoughts","excerpt":"I took the knife at night, And pressed the blade against my skin, And thought if only I could die, Maybe then at least I'd win. And if I won, what would I gain? Release from temporary pain, Until…","text":"I took the knife at night, And pressed the blade against my skin, And thought if only I could die, Maybe then at least I'd win. And if I won, what would I gain? Release from temporary pain, Until the numbness fades away, And pain's left to take its place."},{"order":27,"slug":"remember","title":"I Remember","excerpt":"When I think of you, In my heart I feel pain, For then I realize, I won't see you again. Fondly I think back, To childhood memories, When you were much younger, And had more energy. Back when you…","text":"When I think of you, In my heart I feel pain, For then I realize, I won't see you again. Fondly I think back, To childhood memories, When you were much younger, And had more energy. Back when you could cook a meal, And could get up and walk, When you could sit there in your chair all day, And do nothing but talk. I remember road trips, Driving for many miles, Riding in the car for hours, Just to see your smile. I remember being upset, When I found out you would die, And I'd give anything, If I could just have said goodbye. I want you to know that I love you, And I want you to know this too: I will never forget you, You're special, and I miss you."},{"order":28,"slug":"distraction","title":"Distraction","excerpt":"The days we were together, Were the best I ever knew, And if you weren't there with me, I'm not sure what I'd do. Each day was a little better, So fun it can't be explained, In the aftermath of y…","text":"The days we were together, Were the best I ever knew, And if you weren't there with me, I'm not sure what I'd do. Each day was a little better, So fun it can't be explained, In the aftermath of your presence, I'm left wanting to see you again. But even though the world, Was slowly crashing down around me, You were by my side, And helped forgetfulness surround me. You live too far away, For us to go out or date, And even if you lived next door, We still could not relate. Even though I love so much, I can never have you, Circumstances beyond control, There's nothing I can do. Though we cannot be together, Still, at least I wish, I could see you more often, Because you're so fun to be with."},{"order":29,"slug":"destroyer","title":"The Destroyer","excerpt":"Suffocate me with words of hate, Drown me in feelings of scorn, Choke me with your evil thoughts, Smother me 'till I can take no more. Asphyxiate my happiness, Take away its breath, Pound the nai…","text":"Suffocate me with words of hate, Drown me in feelings of scorn, Choke me with your evil thoughts, Smother me 'till I can take no more. Asphyxiate my happiness, Take away its breath, Pound the nails into its skin, Beat it near to death. Remove the blindfold from my eyes, Tell me what I see, Erase the joy, erase the love, I followed so carelessly. Tie the rope around my neck, And watch me take the fall, Poison me with bitter lies, Ignore my heart's loudest call. Burn the structure of my love, And set my life on fire, Destroy everything like you said you wouldn't, And take my life, you liar."},{"order":30,"slug":"scars","title":"Scars","excerpt":"Skin is thin and unbroken, Like words of hate, left unspoken, Until the blade of conflict cuts, The skin that spreads, as opened up. The blood flows out like crimson streams, Surrounds and drowns…","text":"Skin is thin and unbroken, Like words of hate, left unspoken, Until the blade of conflict cuts, The skin that spreads, as opened up. The blood flows out like crimson streams, Surrounds and drowns the strongest screams, Until the river Red runs dry, All else is left alone to die. The wound, it slowly closes up, And mends until it closes shut, It hides the pain it felt before, And waits for pain that's left in store. Scars appear where wounds once healed, And still reveal where holes were sealed, Remind of times of massive loss, When losing canceled out the cost. The only thing prolonging pain, Are memories inside the brain, That if erased, would put to rest, Reminders of the pain that's left."},{"order":31,"slug":"clone","title":"Clone","excerpt":"I see myself in another place, And see a person with my face, Who looks and acts and talks like me, Compared to me, fits perfectly. As I watch, I see it's me, It's how I felt, internally, It's me…","text":"I see myself in another place, And see a person with my face, Who looks and acts and talks like me, Compared to me, fits perfectly. As I watch, I see it's me, It's how I felt, internally, It's me as I traveled through life, It's every day and every night. As I watch, I am sucked in, I'm more absorbed than I was then, I become an addict of my life, What it was like fades out of sight. I watch as people smash my dreams, Attack and blast all my feelings, Rip my heart out of my chest, Ignite and burn all of the rest. I watch as I am beaten down, I watch myself fall to the ground, I watch myself do stupid things, I watch and cannot make it change. And as I watch, I'm filled with rage, I cannot break out of this cage, I cannot seem to stop myself, From helping cause the pain I felt. At once I'm taken to a place, I meet with myself face to face, I see the pain that I have caused, And see the things that I have lost. Time slows down, goes in slow-motion, And in a blur of pure emotion, I beat myself until I bleed, And keep on beating mercilessly. I hate myself for my mistakes, For times when I believed what's fake, For all the times that I was blind, For when screwed up all the time. And as I think of everything, That I've done wrong, I stop thinking, And let myself go wild with strife, Until I end my very life. The world goes black and fades away, I'm taken to another place, I look around and I'm alone, With no one left except my clone. There's nothing left, except for me, There's nothing left that I can see, There's nothing left to care about, Except to find a new way out. I watched my own self-destruction, I watched as my life turned to nothing, I watched the pieces fall apart, Then laughed as pain began to start. From here on out, I have to try, To bring my dead soul back to life, To give back feeling and resurrect, The body of my life that's left."},{"order":32,"slug":"iknow","title":"I Know","excerpt":"I know how you feel, I've been there so many times, I know what it's like to hate yourself, And do nothing all day but cry. I know how bad it hurts, When someone plays with your heart, But just l…","text":"I know how you feel, I've been there so many times, I know what it's like to hate yourself, And do nothing all day but cry. I know how bad it hurts, When someone plays with your heart, But just like the Fragile says, I won't let you fall apart. I know that things are rough, But remember, I'm here for you, Things WILL get better, Trust me, they always do. I know how life can beat you down, But you have to get back up, If you don't, you'll never win, And wouldn't that just suck? I know that you feel worthless, But you know that can't be true, If it were I wouldn't love you, But luckily I do."},{"order":33,"slug":"true","title":"True Perfection","excerpt":"Last night I experienced perfection, Everything was perfect between us, The only way it could be better, Would be if she could have seen us. I was happy, you were happy, We loved each other so mu…","text":"Last night I experienced perfection, Everything was perfect between us, The only way it could be better, Would be if she could have seen us. I was happy, you were happy, We loved each other so much, I fought to stay forever, To live my dreams, but had no luck. It was the perfect world, The perfect place, the perfect scene, The place that was so perfect, I couldn't believe it wasn't a dream. And even though I can't go back, At least it was escape, At least for once forgot the past, At least forgot my hate. But things are getting better, I love this twist of fate, It's almost like a dream, From which I pray I never wake."},{"order":34,"slug":"ascension","title":"Ascension","excerpt":"The young man who feels so old, Had stumbled through his life, He tried to do what he was told, But never did things right. He did the best he could, But failure always brought him down, He tried…","text":"The young man who feels so old, Had stumbled through his life, He tried to do what he was told, But never did things right. He did the best he could, But failure always brought him down, He tried to smile like he should, But all he did was frown. He blindly gave his love away, When judgment was masked by desire, The heart he wished he hadn't gave, Was broken by a liar. And throughout his experience, He learned to hate himself, Vainly tried making sense of it, But confusion was all he felt. Then one day to his surprise, He found someone like him, Who also hated life, And it attracted him right then. He found someone who could relate, To everything he'd been through, Who knew what it was like to hate, Who liked what he was into. He found the perfect one, Who made his sadness disappear, The one who was so fun, She took his mind off all his fear. He found her nearly dead, At the end of her rope, Hanging by a tiny thread, With barely any hope. He remembered way back when, He felt exactly the same way, Times his hope was growing thin, And could not last another day. He remembered wishing for, One person to really care, Someone who loved him more, Who always would be there. He realized that she needed him, And also that he'd need her, So he promised her right then, That he would never leave her. He loved her deeply with his heart, And said he'd always care, That even when they're far apart, That he'd always be there. And so he wrote this poem for her, Because he loved her so, He loved her more than anything, And wanted her to know."},{"order":35,"slug":"nightlight","title":"Nightlight","excerpt":"Love bursts forth, Like rays of light, A candle in darkness, Piercing the night. Surrounding my love, The warm glow so soft, Light like a bulb, That never turns off. Light of the night, Flowing w…","text":"Love bursts forth, Like rays of light, A candle in darkness, Piercing the night. Surrounding my love, The warm glow so soft, Light like a bulb, That never turns off. Light of the night, Flowing with hope, Bright as sunlight, Hitting the snow. Reason for fighting, To make it closer, Fighting to get there, Before it's over. Calling to me, Spawning desire, I give way and melt, Like ice near a fire. I melt and become, Cool liquid flowing, Attracted to light, And other things glowing. As cool water nears, It turns into mist, Becomes one with the light, As the two co-exist. Antithetical beings, Bonded together, To live as one, With each other forever."},{"order":36,"slug":"iloveyou","title":"I Love You","excerpt":"With my every breath, With all I have left, From the deepest depths, Of my heart, I love you. With all of my strength, With ten miles' length, Every thought I think, I think that I love you. For…","text":"With my every breath, With all I have left, From the deepest depths, Of my heart, I love you. With all of my strength, With ten miles' length, Every thought I think, I think that I love you. For the length of forever, As long as we're together, Through good and bad weather, For always, I love you. Until the very end of days, Until God takes my breath away, Until death separates our ways, Until then, I love you. When no one is there, When you think no one cares, When love seems too rare, Remember, I love you. When everything's gone, When all has withdrawn, When hopelessness dawns, Don't forget, I love you. When you fall down, When your dreams come unwound, When hope can't be found, Be happy, I love you. When you make mistakes, When you're filled with hate, When you're old and gray, Even then, I'll love you."},{"order":37,"slug":"forever","title":"Forever","excerpt":"How long is forever? And will it ever end? And if it never does, Then how did it ever begin? When forever comes, How will we know it's here? I guess we'll never know, Before it comes we'll disapp…","text":"How long is forever? And will it ever end? And if it never does, Then how did it ever begin? When forever comes, How will we know it's here? I guess we'll never know, Before it comes we'll disappear. If forever never ends, Then we're always in-between, Eternity behind us, And still more to be seen. When we live, we run a race, In which we'll never win, A race that has no finish, A race that never ends. And if we'll never see, The finish of the race, Then what's the point of running? It seems like such a waste. But I will keep on running, To see what's left in store, Until I run no longer, Or lose what I run for."},{"order":38,"slug":"giveme","title":"Give Me","excerpt":"Give me your hate, Give me your fear, Give me your worries, And they'll disappear. Give me your sadness, Give me your pain, Give me your storms, And I'll stop the rain. Give me the hurt, Give me…","text":"Give me your hate, Give me your fear, Give me your worries, And they'll disappear. Give me your sadness, Give me your pain, Give me your storms, And I'll stop the rain. Give me the hurt, Give me the shit, Give me it all, I'll get rid of it. Give me the pieces, Of your broken heart, Give me your world, As it falls apart. Give me your problems, I'll bear them for you, Give me your life, When there's nothing to lose. Give me your love, And you'll have mine forever, No matter the problem, We'll fix it together."},{"order":39,"slug":"questioning","title":"Questioning Good","excerpt":"Everything is going well, How long until it falls? I finally have everything, When will I lose it all? Can this be reality? Or just a euphoric delusion? Can things be this good? Or is it just an…","text":"Everything is going well, How long until it falls? I finally have everything, When will I lose it all? Can this be reality? Or just a euphoric delusion? Can things be this good? Or is it just an illusion? Should I be concerned? Should I worry about something? Am I really held back? Or am I chained to nothing? And if I'm chained to nothing, How can I be set free? If my fears aren't real, Then how can they control me?"},{"order":40,"slug":"it","title":"It","excerpt":"From whence it was, and whence it came, And since it was, was not the same, And since the name, was spoken back, The things it loved, were turned to black. And black they were, though black is no…","text":"From whence it was, and whence it came, And since it was, was not the same, And since the name, was spoken back, The things it loved, were turned to black. And black they were, though black is not, Black as could be, before it's stopped, And left to be, held back before, The words were shaped, to metaphors. And as they were, they were like rain, Dyed red with blood, to hide the stain, That eats away, at one's white life, Until it's dyed, with a sharp knife. As it is, and as it was, Was not the same, but just because, The stains are gone, problems still live, Complications, relative. The more it gives, the more it seems, The more it gives away its dreams, And loses out, on what is left, While trying to enjoy the best. And rest for then another day, To come again, for chance to say, The way to test, is left without, The way to find, the shortest route."},{"order":41,"slug":"wonder","title":"Wonder","excerpt":"I shiver in the moonlight, And look up at the stars, My body is so cold, Without the warmth that is your arms. I sit here and I wonder, If I'll make it through the week, But going on is harder, W…","text":"I shiver in the moonlight, And look up at the stars, My body is so cold, Without the warmth that is your arms. I sit here and I wonder, If I'll make it through the week, But going on is harder, When your future is so bleak. And all around I see, Reminders of the past, Reminders that the good times, Never seem to last. I wonder how your promises, Can so quickly disappear, You said you'd always be there, But I look and you're not here. You said you'd never let me fall, But I did; I fell for you, And now that you've gone away, I don't know what to do. Life doesn't seem worth living, Since we're no longer together, I wish I could just lay down, And go to sleep forever. And in my sleep I'd dream, Of good days done and gone, Days that were so perfect, That nothing could go wrong. I never thought I'd see the day, That we would fall apart, That love would pass us by, And with it, take my heart. I wonder why when we got close, We were then pulled asunder, But I guess I'll never know, I'll just be left to wonder."},{"order":42,"slug":"regret","title":"Regretfully Apologetic","excerpt":"I'm sorry for the things I've said, You know I didn't mean them And this whole time that you've been gone, I've prayed I was just dreaming And though we've done each other wrong, You still give m…","text":"I'm sorry for the things I've said, You know I didn't mean them And this whole time that you've been gone, I've prayed I was just dreaming And though we've done each other wrong, You still give my life meaning My ears still ring with echoes of, Love songs you were singing"},{"order":43,"slug":"sorry","title":"Sorry","excerpt":"I'm sorry that I get upset, Whenever you do wrong, And I'm sorry that our time together, Never lasts that long. I'm sorry that I love you, So much that when you fail, To spend your time with me,…","text":"I'm sorry that I get upset, Whenever you do wrong, And I'm sorry that our time together, Never lasts that long. I'm sorry that I love you, So much that when you fail, To spend your time with me, I make your life a living hell. I'm sorry I enjoy, The pleasure your body provides, And if I said I didn't like it, Then I'd be telling a lie. I'm sorry that I love you so, That I can't live without you, I'm sorry that I care so much, I always think about you. I'm sorry I tell you I love you, So much it's like the song from Barney, But the scary thing to me is, True love's not having to say you're sorry."},{"order":44,"slug":"wish","title":"Wish","excerpt":"I'm so empty here without you, All I do is think about you, All I want is your sweet touch, I want and need your love so much. I miss the good times that we shared, I wish you acted like you care…","text":"I'm so empty here without you, All I do is think about you, All I want is your sweet touch, I want and need your love so much. I miss the good times that we shared, I wish you acted like you cared, I wish I wasn't so alone, I wish that I could just go home. I wish that we were still together, And that we'd stay that way forever, I wish that I would just not cry, And in a way that I would die. But the wish I wish the most, Is that we could again be close, That again you could be near, And that I could just have you here. But though I wish upon the stars, The sun and moon, we're still apart, I miss my nightlight, as I've said, So now I bump into my bed."},{"order":45,"slug":"sleep","title":"Sleep","excerpt":"When life overwhelms, In sleep, I find peace, It's the one place in life, Where I find relief. The one place where I, Have nothing to fear, The place where my problems, All disappear. Sleep is li…","text":"When life overwhelms, In sleep, I find peace, It's the one place in life, Where I find relief. The one place where I, Have nothing to fear, The place where my problems, All disappear. Sleep is like, Temporary death, Except that your body, Still has its breath. And in sleep you may dream, Of the way things should be, The way that it all, Fits so perfectly. When I drift away, What I wish to keep, I find in my dreams, So I think that I'll just sleep."},{"order":46,"slug":"delusion","title":"Delusion","excerpt":"I've been thinking, you know, About us, this, and that, About how much I miss you, And how much I want you back. For now, we exist in a single place; The land inside my head, Illusions of us keep…","text":"I've been thinking, you know, About us, this, and that, About how much I miss you, And how much I want you back. For now, we exist in a single place; The land inside my head, Illusions of us keep me alive, But my inside's all but dead. Broken promises in my mind, Words of love, turned to stone, What I loved most, taken away, Like always, left alone. My tank is now on empty, My shallow soul so hollow, The void where you once were, no longer, Gives me signs to follow. I can't go on, for I am being, Eaten from the inside out, By a love that yearns for you, And with you, can't do without. I should release my fantasies, I guess, And purify my thoughts, Erase the memories of you, For you can't regain the lost."},{"order":47,"slug":"absolutes","title":"Absolutes","excerpt":"As the sun sets every day, So do my dreams fade away. As the wind of winter blows, So’s the door of my dreams closed. As the stars refuse to die, With the dead my wishes lie. As the weeds in gard…","text":"As the sun sets every day, So do my dreams fade away. As the wind of winter blows, So’s the door of my dreams closed. As the stars refuse to die, With the dead my wishes lie. As the weeds in gardens grow, The growth of my problem’s not slowed. As the world, for now, still turns, My love for her forever burns."},{"order":48,"slug":"confessions","title":"Confessions of a Liar","excerpt":"Looking, I see reminders, Reminders of things long past, Reminders of us. I try to block the memories, But it's hard to ignore the loss of... Such a wonderful person. So I say I don't care, Becau…","text":"Looking, I see reminders, Reminders of things long past, Reminders of us. I try to block the memories, But it's hard to ignore the loss of... Such a wonderful person. So I say I don't care, Because sometimes caring, Does more harm than good. I say I don't care, Because it's the hard way out, Disguised as the easy way out. If I don't care, Then I don't have to deal with it, But if I don't care, why do I feel this way? You broke your promises, And for that you are a liar, But I'm also a liar for lying to myself. I want you back, But wanting you and not having you is worse than anything, So I try not to want you. But it doesn't work, Because my love was true love... True love never dies, it just hides. So I can lie to myself, And I can lie to you too, But I guess that it makes me no better than you. So when I act like I don't care, Remember that I'm lying... Trying to save myself from pain."},{"order":49,"slug":"falsehope","title":"False Hope","excerpt":"I hate to ask, Because if I don't, Then you can't say no, And I can't be rejected. I can live inside a false hope that maybe, Just maybe, Your love is still hidden away, Like treasures of ages pa…","text":"I hate to ask, Because if I don't, Then you can't say no, And I can't be rejected. I can live inside a false hope that maybe, Just maybe, Your love is still hidden away, Like treasures of ages past. The false hope is what I cling to, The last chance that perhaps I can have you back, Someday soon, But even some distant day would be better than no day. So I won't ask, So I can't feel the sting of rejection once more. But I'm already so hurt, What would a little more pain do? It would do nothing, of course. I could gamble. I could ask and maybe you would say yes, That there is still chance. That there is still hope. But if the answer was no, That never would we have a chance, What would I do? Of course... I would remember. I would remember how strongly you felt before, How much you loved me and how strongly you clung to that feeling. That changed, So who's to say this won't too? So once again, I am left clinging to a false hope. A false hope that perhaps, You'll change your mind once more."},{"order":50,"slug":"yourfault","title":"Your Fault","excerpt":"Look into my eyes, See the pain? It's your fault. Listen to my voice, Hear the pain? It's your fault. Touch my shaking hands, Feel the pain? It's your fault. Look down at my wrists, See the pain?…","text":"Look into my eyes, See the pain? It's your fault. Listen to my voice, Hear the pain? It's your fault. Touch my shaking hands, Feel the pain? It's your fault. Look down at my wrists, See the pain? It's your fault. Lick my open wounds, Taste the pain? It's your fault. Sniff my burning love, Smell the pain? It's your fault. Feel my words of hate. Know the pain. It's all your fault."},{"order":51,"slug":"thanks","title":"Thanks for Everything","excerpt":"I'd like to take this time, To thank you. To thank you for everything you've done, To, and for me. Thanks for giving me time alone. It sure is wonderful. I thought I had a lot of time alone befor…","text":"I'd like to take this time, To thank you. To thank you for everything you've done, To, and for me. Thanks for giving me time alone. It sure is wonderful. I thought I had a lot of time alone before, But this is incredible. I never knew you could be this alone, Because I've never been this alone in my life. Thanks for making me single. I never knew being single was so great, And I never liked it before. But I feel so free... If there was anyone to flirt with, I could. If there was anything I wanted to do apart from you, I could do it. I'm like a bird with broken wings, In an open cage. I may be free to go, But what good is it when I can't? Thank you for giving me inspiration to write. I thought I wrote a lot before, But since you've left writing pours out like... Rain from a thunderstorm. Or, cursing from a sailor's mouth. Curses I wish to hurl at you, But can't, Because I'm already saying to you... Thanks for everything."},{"order":52,"slug":"oops","title":"Oops","excerpt":"I lay down and rest, Like my finger resting on the trigger. Oops, my finger slipped, Like your love when it slipped away from me... Oops, I tripped. I was just running to catch your love, And bes…","text":"I lay down and rest, Like my finger resting on the trigger. Oops, my finger slipped, Like your love when it slipped away from me... Oops, I tripped. I was just running to catch your love, And besides... I didn't know it had fallen so far down. Oops, I went too deep. Looks like I was carried away in the moment, Like when my love got carried away, And went too deep for you. Oops, I forgot to breathe. Look what you do to me... You take my mind off the important things, And I get careless. Oops, I tripped again. But this time I won't fall very far, Because I'm at the end of my rope, As well as the end of the rope of your love. Oops, I was distracted, And I took too much. Looks like too much of a good thing can kill you. But apparently... So can too little."},{"order":53,"slug":"difficult","title":"Difficult","excerpt":"Many things are difficult in life, But very few things are beyond difficult. Seeing you love another as you loved me, Falls into the second category. The coldness I feel, is another's warmth. The…","text":"Many things are difficult in life, But very few things are beyond difficult. Seeing you love another as you loved me, Falls into the second category. The coldness I feel, is another's warmth. The sadness I feel, is another's joy. The hunger I feel, is another's feast. The pain that I feel, is another's pleasure."},{"order":54,"slug":"donttell","title":"Don't Tell Me","excerpt":"Don't tell me not to be sad. You don't know what it's like. You were everything to me, And I lost you. I lost everything. Don't tell me not to be sad, When you are sitting right in front of me. H…","text":"Don't tell me not to be sad. You don't know what it's like. You were everything to me, And I lost you. I lost everything. Don't tell me not to be sad, When you are sitting right in front of me. How can I not be sad, When what I can't have is right in front of me? I try to hold back the tears, Like I try holding back my love for you, Thinking it will make things better. But it doesn't... So don't tell me not to be sad."},{"order":55,"slug":"goodfriend","title":"The Good Friend","excerpt":"I try to be nice, And bear the pain, But what's the point? I'll never have you back anyway. But I'll just be a good friend. You could use one. The pain will only get worse, But I'll bear it for y…","text":"I try to be nice, And bear the pain, But what's the point? I'll never have you back anyway. But I'll just be a good friend. You could use one. The pain will only get worse, But I'll bear it for your sake. Where does one draw the line, Between their own well-being, And a friendship? Is it even right to? Even if it is, I'll stay. You'll need me Once everything Falls Apart"},{"order":56,"slug":"ridofyou","title":"Rid of You","excerpt":"You know I'd get rid of you if I could. But I can't seem to get rid of you, Like you got rid of me. So I take my hands off your neck, And stop choking you. As I let you go, In my mind, You die. I…","text":"You know I'd get rid of you if I could. But I can't seem to get rid of you, Like you got rid of me. So I take my hands off your neck, And stop choking you. As I let you go, In my mind, You die. I've finally gotten rid of you."},{"order":57,"slug":"without","title":"Without You","excerpt":"My hands are lonely, Without yours to hold. My eyes are vacant, Without yours staring back. My arms are cold, Without your body to warm them. My ears are dead, Without your voice to give them lif…","text":"My hands are lonely, Without yours to hold. My eyes are vacant, Without yours staring back. My arms are cold, Without your body to warm them. My ears are dead, Without your voice to give them life. My lips are burning, Without yours to put the fire out. My heart is screaming, crying... Without you."},{"order":58,"slug":"froze","title":"The Day my Heart Froze Over","excerpt":"Three times since, and three times then, Three times to realize I can't win. And now I see it's three strikes out, There's nothing left to care about. For me, caring brings only pain, I cannot ta…","text":"Three times since, and three times then, Three times to realize I can't win. And now I see it's three strikes out, There's nothing left to care about. For me, caring brings only pain, I cannot take that risk again. And so, I'll hide my love away, And save it for a future day, A day in many, many years, When time has dried up all my tears. The day I find someone who cares, Who will be there through my despair. And though you three have broken trust, In my heart there always will be \"us.\" But on the day the third strike dawned, I chose that day to not go on. Today's the day, in mind I chose, To love no more, my heart has froze."},{"order":59,"slug":"parting","title":"Parting Ways","excerpt":"And so, I see, it's come to this, Fate's gone against our strongest wish, And though I wish that you were here, I cannot make you reappear. But even if to me you came, Things would never be the s…","text":"And so, I see, it's come to this, Fate's gone against our strongest wish, And though I wish that you were here, I cannot make you reappear. But even if to me you came, Things would never be the same, I'd just be left to wonder when, The day would come, you'd leave again. I know we both have made mistakes, But I've had all that I can take, And you can't say I never loved, For on that, you know nothing of. And though I did enjoy the days, We were together, let's part ways, For hiding feelings felt for you, Is easier for me to do."},{"order":60,"slug":"mercurian","title":"Mercurian","excerpt":"Through distances I feel you, Even though you've left, And things may now be perfect, But soon they'll be a mess. For underneath the surface, Complications lurk, And even though you might deny, Y…","text":"Through distances I feel you, Even though you've left, And things may now be perfect, But soon they'll be a mess. For underneath the surface, Complications lurk, And even though you might deny, You know that it won't work. It failed to work the first time, Why then should it work now? You may say you've changed, But simple logic won't allow. Of course you've changed, that's the thing, You're bound to change once more, Insecure, unstable, In your mercurial core. You never get to see him, For you live too far apart, Try not to get attached, Lest he break your fragile heart. I know I cannot stop you, But whenever it ends, Know that I'll be here to help you, I'll be your best friend."},{"order":61,"slug":"million","title":"Million","excerpt":"A million different things Spinning through my mind A million thoughts I wish to put into words But can't Even if I could I could not tell them to her I am silenced And restrained A million curse…","text":"A million different things Spinning through my mind A million thoughts I wish to put into words But can't Even if I could I could not tell them to her I am silenced And restrained A million curses For a million broken promises A million violent fantasies Crossing my dreams each night A million ways to kill A million ways it'll never work out A million ways to die A million voices laughing Laughing at her pathetic attempts Laughing as she cries Laughing as she loses her most valuable possession One million words of hate piercing like daggers One million lies breaking my heart Into one million jagged edges One million kicks to her self esteem As I laugh One million daggers in her heart As she loses all as I did."},{"order":62,"slug":"words","title":"Words","excerpt":"Your words when put, Together form, The clouds that then, Produce the storms, That wear away, My confidence, Until my patience, Has been spent, And as they leave, The aftermath, Is harder than, T…","text":"Your words when put, Together form, The clouds that then, Produce the storms, That wear away, My confidence, Until my patience, Has been spent, And as they leave, The aftermath, Is harder than, The former path."},{"order":63,"slug":"runner","title":"Runner-Up","excerpt":"Second best at most, But mostly second best, And lying words so often heard, Don't give my patience rest. So I try to ignore them, But the problem only grows, I fight the hate with love, Yet I st…","text":"Second best at most, But mostly second best, And lying words so often heard, Don't give my patience rest. So I try to ignore them, But the problem only grows, I fight the hate with love, Yet I still lose my repose. If I somehow was able, To attenuate my pain, And still I felt like this, There'd be no one else to blame. However as it stands, If any longer I'm ignored, I'm giving up on friends, For they're too much to afford."},{"order":64,"slug":"selfish","title":"Selfish?","excerpt":"I look and all I f-cking see Are memories of you and me Reminding of pain carved into A fading memory of you What you don't want, you cannot miss The damage done cannot be fixed Much less by a fi…","text":"I look and all I f-cking see Are memories of you and me Reminding of pain carved into A fading memory of you What you don't want, you cannot miss The damage done cannot be fixed Much less by a five lettered word Which in this case should be a verb However it's simply a lie A noun expressed within a sigh If you were sorry, you would help Someone other than yourself And selfish though to some I sound I'd like to now turn that around For which of us neglected feelings? Promises, and other dealings? Who here broke the other's heart? And who left who to fall apart? Who betrayed their \"bestest friend?\" And brought their life near to an end? Her you see, I broke no trust All I wanted, was her love But such a simple thing as this Was given to a stupid prick But after all, it's just a girl There's many of them in this world There's always more fish in the sea But it doesn't matter, when none are for me..."},{"order":65,"slug":"shattered","title":"Shattered Existence","excerpt":"Never have I needed help I've always made it through myself But this time I doubt I can take it And no longer can I fake it No longer can I cry at night I've lost my strength and will to fight I…","text":"Never have I needed help I've always made it through myself But this time I doubt I can take it And no longer can I fake it No longer can I cry at night I've lost my strength and will to fight I just can't take it anymore I hate this life, I hate this world I hate how people always leave me How girls are so apt to deceive me And the way that life repeats My tragedies, and my defeats If this is how the rest will be Then now would be the time to leave Take the key and turn, unlock Slowly open up Death's box Bring this hell unto an end And break me before I can bend Flashing pictures, life and dreams Until from this body I'm free"},{"order":66,"slug":"wasted","title":"Wasted","excerpt":"Wasted so many tears Crying over you, Wasted so many days Believing what's not true. I wasted so many nights With you on my mind, Wasted so much of life With you by my side. Wasted so long with y…","text":"Wasted so many tears Crying over you, Wasted so many days Believing what's not true. I wasted so many nights With you on my mind, Wasted so much of life With you by my side. Wasted so long with you, Living in a lie, If I could take it back I would, And let you pass by. I wasted so much of my time Letting you control me, Finally I've broken free, And I'm healing slowly. I wasted so much love Loving that which was not real, I no longer love you, Now I hope you know how it feels."},{"order":67,"slug":"changed","title":"Changed","excerpt":"The blood that flowed, From my wrist, The tears I cried, My eyes did miss, The pain that was, A hidden gift, The trials that, Strengthened my grip. Experience, Through time I gained, Blessings we…","text":"The blood that flowed, From my wrist, The tears I cried, My eyes did miss, The pain that was, A hidden gift, The trials that, Strengthened my grip. Experience, Through time I gained, Blessings were, Disguised by pain, The spill that rendered, My life stained, Is no more, For things have changed. The times my fingers, Pointed blame. Back at myself, Are gone again, Happiness, No longer feigned, I wear the smile, Now my name."},{"order":68,"slug":"dive","title":"Dive","excerpt":"Reflection in the water, The face inside that's me, Ripples break the surface, Like waves among the sea. Rain falls down in torrents, Lightning lights the sky, Dreams may fall and crumble, But wi…","text":"Reflection in the water, The face inside that's me, Ripples break the surface, Like waves among the sea. Rain falls down in torrents, Lightning lights the sky, Dreams may fall and crumble, But wishes never die. Stepping off, descent, Ends within a splash, Swallowed by the depths, Of the foamy wash. Underwater shelter, Save me from the world, Floating in the liquid, All the while curled. Ocean pulls me close, The warmth, it slowly grows, The Ocean understands me, It's the only one that knows."},{"order":69,"slug":"aide","title":"Malicious Aide","excerpt":"Skin is made of razorblades Eyes are cold as steel Touching her that day created Pain that I still feel. Slicing fingers, hands, and arms Harming me beyond repair Stumbling backwards, far in shoc…","text":"Skin is made of razorblades Eyes are cold as steel Touching her that day created Pain that I still feel. Slicing fingers, hands, and arms Harming me beyond repair Stumbling backwards, far in shock All the while, unaware. Focus back reality Finding myself torn apart Watching happiness once had As quickly it departs. Beauty I once trusted Was not what it had seemed Light surrounding her, not love Just blades in light that gleamed. I realize dangerous she is Though disguised as help Get away from me, foul whore Just leave me to myself. Your mirage of full support I can now see through Distorted lies then form the truth I see I don't need you. In the place of happiness Was you holding the knife That stabs me in the back no more For you're not in my life."},{"order":70,"slug":"payback","title":"Payback","excerpt":"I care not what you do I care not where you go I only care about the fact That I told you so. Times when I was crying Never once lifted your brow And now that we have switched positions Guess who…","text":"I care not what you do I care not where you go I only care about the fact That I told you so. Times when I was crying Never once lifted your brow And now that we have switched positions Guess who's laughing now. When you said you loved me It all was just an act But now I'm having all my fun While you're getting paid back."},{"order":71,"slug":"interstice","title":"Interstice","excerpt":"On lonely nights I sit, And trace my thoughts across the sky, And watch them form the visions, Of the lives of you and I. I dream of days to come, When the distance disappears, And thank the Lord…","text":"On lonely nights I sit, And trace my thoughts across the sky, And watch them form the visions, Of the lives of you and I. I dream of days to come, When the distance disappears, And thank the Lord in Heaven, For each second that it nears. I know it in my heart, That you're the one He's sent, I'll know I lived a good life, If with you it's spent. So I close my eyes As I invite my slumber over And contentedly I sigh, As I realize we're one day closer."},{"order":72,"slug":"future","title":"Future","excerpt":"In the gentle depth of introspection I concede, That in the wreck of my defects in you I find a need. My constant thoughts that center on a future filled with you, Are nothing next to the effects…","text":"In the gentle depth of introspection I concede, That in the wreck of my defects in you I find a need. My constant thoughts that center on a future filled with you, Are nothing next to the effects of finding out they're true. My love for you, try as I might, just cannot be expressed, Caught in the wind of love again, you are my one request. I yearn for days ahead when I instead can hold you close, The days we'll be together for forever unlike most."},{"order":73,"slug":"sardonic","title":"The Sardonic","excerpt":"Come with us Run with us And all the fires of Hell Dumb like us Succumb like us Before the timely knell Used like us Abused like us We made your problems swell Mused like us Confused like us But…","text":"Come with us Run with us And all the fires of Hell Dumb like us Succumb like us Before the timely knell Used like us Abused like us We made your problems swell Mused like us Confused like us But no one else can tell Try like us And die like us Within your final yell Cry like us Imply like us That you already fell"},{"order":74,"slug":"bleeding","title":"Bleeding","excerpt":"I feel myself inside Bleeding, A permanent wound upon my heart, The gash spread wide. With each beat of my heart I lose a part of myself. My blood, my life Drains before me. It’s said that what’s…","text":"I feel myself inside Bleeding, A permanent wound upon my heart, The gash spread wide. With each beat of my heart I lose a part of myself. My blood, my life Drains before me. It’s said that what’s gone Cannot be re-gained And there are pieces Pieces of my heart Missing. The empty spaces ache, And ache further as thoughts come to me Thoughts of the past Stabbing at my heart Creating further pain. My heart is beaten, Scarred, swollen, Bruised, And wounded. It cries out for someone, But its pleas go unanswered. No one comes to stop the bleeding Or to heal the wounds And fix the broken heart. It is simply left Alone Bleeding."},{"order":75,"slug":"riddle","title":"Riddle","excerpt":"It comes when not needed, And flees when it is, Makes a grand entrance, Then leaves with a kiss, It starts off simple, Then quickly unfolds, It’s the worst thing to happen, To some, I’ve been tol…","text":"It comes when not needed, And flees when it is, Makes a grand entrance, Then leaves with a kiss, It starts off simple, Then quickly unfolds, It’s the worst thing to happen, To some, I’ve been told. It can be either the wind, That allows you to soar, Or the hunger inside you, That begs you for more, The light of your life, Or darkness of death, But nevertheless, You won’t soon forget, It flies like a butterfly, And stings like a shot, Leaves when you beckon it, Comes when said to stop, Of course by now you’re wondering, Just what I’m speaking of, And mournfully I answer: The monster we call love."},{"order":76,"slug":"excuse","title":"Excuse Me","excerpt":"Excuse me while I vomit While I spill my insides here before you Excuse me while I throw up The words and feelings placed upon me Please excuse me while I turn myself inside-out While I show the…","text":"Excuse me while I vomit While I spill my insides here before you Excuse me while I throw up The words and feelings placed upon me Please excuse me while I turn myself inside-out While I show the world what lies within me For anyone who has the courage to look Anyone who has the strength to see And realize I can't take this shit anymore I can't take much more of it It's making me sick So please excuse me."},{"order":77,"slug":"igneus","title":"Igneus Velius","excerpt":"First a sting, Then a burn, Then an unexpected turn Euphoria Flowing through veins Washes away The strongest pains And then of course Like always, it Returns to me Bit by bit","text":"First a sting, Then a burn, Then an unexpected turn Euphoria Flowing through veins Washes away The strongest pains And then of course Like always, it Returns to me Bit by bit"},{"order":78,"slug":"stupidity","title":"Stupidity","excerpt":"Ignorance lifted up, high on a pedestal The dumb are treated as gods, I may not be that popular, But I'm glad to be what they're not. The happiest fools the whole world over, For ignorance is bli…","text":"Ignorance lifted up, high on a pedestal The dumb are treated as gods, I may not be that popular, But I'm glad to be what they're not. The happiest fools the whole world over, For ignorance is bliss, All things valued greatly by them May as well be piss. Leeching off the rest of us Who exercise our minds, They use not any of their sight, They may as well be blind. Eradicate, obliterate, Abundant numbers bound, To feed and steal like parasites And tear our greatness down."},{"order":79,"slug":"nottoday","title":"Not Today","excerpt":"Death slides close to me, I say, \"Not today, friend, Not today.\"","text":"Death slides close to me, I say, \"Not today, friend, Not today.\""},{"order":80,"slug":"shallow","title":"Shallow","excerpt":"Shallow is shallow Can't see beyond the surface Can't go a little deeper Can't try a little harder Shallow's as shallow as its shadow As shallow as the half empty glass Except... more shallow...…","text":"Shallow is shallow Can't see beyond the surface Can't go a little deeper Can't try a little harder Shallow's as shallow as its shadow As shallow as the half empty glass Except... more shallow... For Shallow is callow, Immature in its perception Immature in its view, Immature, Shallow's you."},{"order":81,"slug":"hypocrite","title":"Hypocrites","excerpt":"I've got an idea! Let's jump to conclusions! When we don't even realize, We're lost in confusion! We're all about freedom, We're free speech's minions, We preach acceptance, But hate your opinion…","text":"I've got an idea! Let's jump to conclusions! When we don't even realize, We're lost in confusion! We're all about freedom, We're free speech's minions, We preach acceptance, But hate your opinions. We judge them before we See what they're about, Talk not with our heads, But only our mouths. We say you should stand up, While we only sit, We're stupid, dumb, F-cking hypocrites. Respect our opinions, We don't respect yours, We're not the least bit consistent, When choosing our wars. When you say what you feel, We must throw our fits, Because we're the dumb F-cking hypocrites."},{"order":82,"slug":"never","title":"Never","excerpt":"Adrift amid desolate water I recollect the depths this surface hides This surface, this thin boundary Lies between the different sides As I think back to when I visited The depths of water Grey,…","text":"Adrift amid desolate water I recollect the depths this surface hides This surface, this thin boundary Lies between the different sides As I think back to when I visited The depths of water Grey, I realize the depth beneath me Is not at all that far away. I feel a tug that pulls me, Ever so slightly down, A force pushes me under And the source I think I've found. It's the world pulling me under, Trying to drown me once again, But this time I have strength; I can't and won't give in. I'm struggling to keep my head up, But the weight's too much to bear, Slowly I begin to sink, But I won't go back there. I'll never sink so low again, I'll never lose my sight, I'll never let things drag me down, I will control my life."},{"order":83,"slug":"phone","title":"The Phone","excerpt":"The phone is silent Idle Awaiting a call It has no other job Just ring, That's all. I am silent Idle Awaiting your call I have no other job Just answer, That's all.","text":"The phone is silent Idle Awaiting a call It has no other job Just ring, That's all. I am silent Idle Awaiting your call I have no other job Just answer, That's all."},{"order":84,"slug":"touch","title":"Just a Touch","excerpt":"It was just a touch A brief moment of contact And even though I didnt know you It changed me Even though you were a stranger You opened my eyes You Looked deep inside of me You saw the problem Co…","text":"It was just a touch A brief moment of contact And even though I didnt know you It changed me Even though you were a stranger You opened my eyes You Looked deep inside of me You saw the problem Corrected my view Repaired my injury And made me anew And even though I didn't know you You gave me a chance You helped With just a touch."},{"order":85,"slug":"HM","title":"H.M. (The Light That Shines Through Rain)","excerpt":"I put it all behind me, But I always turn around, Just when I think it's straightened out, It all turns upside-down. Just when I get back to my feet, The ground on which I stand, Is pulled away f…","text":"I put it all behind me, But I always turn around, Just when I think it's straightened out, It all turns upside-down. Just when I get back to my feet, The ground on which I stand, Is pulled away from me so fast, I don't know where I'll land. Amidst the spinning, tumbling, That this world puts me through, It pauses for a moment, When I think of you. The moments spent with you, I see, are worth the pain, And thus we see the value of, The light that shines through rain."},{"order":86,"slug":"someone","title":"Someone","excerpt":"Head in my hands and heart in the trash the scene so familiar just old and rehashed All that I live for's, Just reasons to laugh, All that surrounds me's All I can't have A hundred, a thousand, A…","text":"Head in my hands and heart in the trash the scene so familiar just old and rehashed All that I live for's, Just reasons to laugh, All that surrounds me's All I can't have A hundred, a thousand, A million or more, Mocking, faces, Knock me to the floor The anguish, the pain, Of faces that swore, To love me, forever, Don't love anymore 'Cause all that I want, And all that I need Is someone to be there At all times for me Someone, somehow Who is able to see The things that I am And the things I could be Someone that appreciates, Somebody that cares, Someone that would always, Try to be there, Someone that looks past The scars that I bear, And loves me for me, Not the clothes that I wear. And it seems that she's always, Always so near, But when I reach for her, She just disappears, And sometimes it seems, That the message is clear, I'll never have her, She'll never be here."},{"order":87,"slug":"recidivism","title":"Recidivism","excerpt":"Maybe I should jump And see who'd catch me if I fell And if nobody did I guess that it'd be just as well. 'Cause if nobody cares Enough to save me from a fall I guess that they won't miss me When…","text":"Maybe I should jump And see who'd catch me if I fell And if nobody did I guess that it'd be just as well. 'Cause if nobody cares Enough to save me from a fall I guess that they won't miss me When they find out I am gone."},{"order":88,"slug":"pieces","title":"Pieces Have Their Place","excerpt":"A puzzle, it seems, Where all pieces have their place, Except the odd piece out. I feel like him, these days. I've tried, but I give up. In this world, I.. just don't fit. It just isn't meant for…","text":"A puzzle, it seems, Where all pieces have their place, Except the odd piece out. I feel like him, these days. I've tried, but I give up. In this world, I.. just don't fit. It just isn't meant for me, This just isn't it. But it's okay, I'm sure I'll deal. No, in fact, I'm sure I will. I just don't care. The ties are being severed And the walls are being built The wire's being run As the old me slowly wilts. I'm disconnecting from the world I'm losing feeling; numb, Forgetting what it is to love, Forgetting where I'm from. But it's okay, I'm sure I'll deal. No, in fact, I'm sure I will. I just don't care. I only have to feel, That which I desire, Filter out the shit, Burn it in the fire. Because... I'm seperate now I'm isolated, finally free I'm in a world that I control, Since you rejected me. But it's okay, It really is. I just don't care."},{"order":89,"slug":"little","title":"A Little Off","excerpt":"It's never quite the way you thought it would be Always a little off Puzzles with imaginary solutions And temporary fixes For temporary complications And things unseen But felt by the heart And t…","text":"It's never quite the way you thought it would be Always a little off Puzzles with imaginary solutions And temporary fixes For temporary complications And things unseen But felt by the heart And thrown to the wayside Discarded Up in flames With the broken dreams The broken wings And things unseen But felt by the heart Guided by night Lost in the dark But you get what you want Though always a little off And not quite what you expected But you want to like it And even though it can't be seen It's felt by the heart So you accept it And the pieces never fit Quite the way they did before Always a little off Not how you thought it would be And not that you can see But felt by the heart Discarded A little off Unseen But felt Not like you Just off A little"},{"order":90,"slug":"throw","title":"Throw It All Away","excerpt":"You've been so blessed with an enlightened way You see the world in varied shades of grey You know it all too very, very well You're forced to keep it to yourself.... You see what others always f…","text":"You've been so blessed with an enlightened way You see the world in varied shades of grey You know it all too very, very well You're forced to keep it to yourself.... You see what others always fail to see You watch them act the way you want to be You know it more than anybody else You're forced to keep it to yourself.... Would you throw it all away? For just a single day? Would you forfeit all you are, Just to get away? Would you turn your back on treasure, And instead, opt to pay? Would you throw it all away? Would you throw it all away? You have what others wish that they could have But it seems that Fate needed a laugh Despite the everything that you have tried The grass is always greener, on the other side You know the things you wish you could forget Ignorance is bliss, and knowledge isn't it So for peace of mind you'd give up all your wealth But you're forced to keep it to yourself.... Will you throw it all away? For just a single day? Will you forfeit all you are, Just to get away? Will you turn your back on treasure, And instead, opt to pay? Will you throw it all away? Will you throw it all away? All you want is to be like everyone else For this you'll even give up your good health Relax, you'll be too dumb to realize The sacrifice you made to win the prize Once you go, there is no turning back But you don't mind, that's just a useless fact You'll no longer see what most don't see \"That's okay, this is what I need.\" So you throw it all away For just a single day You forfeit all you are, Just to get away You turn your back on treasure, And instead you opt to pay You throw it all away You throw it all away"},{"order":91,"slug":"violence","title":"Violence","excerpt":"Push me once more, you'll receive The pain you've inflicted on me I'll beat you till you flow with blood But still, that will not be enough I'll bring my fist back to your face The air you breath…","text":"Push me once more, you'll receive The pain you've inflicted on me I'll beat you till you flow with blood But still, that will not be enough I'll bring my fist back to your face The air you breathe is such a waste My fist completes one more attack Each time it does, I get you back I put both hands around your throat And laugh while you begin to choke Now which one of us is weak? Who now is too afraid to speak? Those feelings they were never mine I was waiting for the right time And now I let you go and laugh For you have tasted half my wraith I would have given all to you But I wanted you to know all through That the power lies with me So don't you ever f-ck with me"},{"order":92,"slug":"redivivus","title":"Redivivus","excerpt":"You can’t see the happiness, Or how much that you’ve helped, You couldn’t see my heart, Or the pain so long it felt. You couldn't see my problems, Or the shit that I went through, For all your he…","text":"You can’t see the happiness, Or how much that you’ve helped, You couldn’t see my heart, Or the pain so long it felt. You couldn't see my problems, Or the shit that I went through, For all your help, for all you've done, I am thanking you."},{"order":93,"slug":"survive","title":"The Will To Survive","excerpt":"Wretched bones and tired look Upon the beaten face Torn flesh that stubbornly Keeps old rags in place Varied shades of grey Cast upon unblinking brow Sullen, sunken eyes Wish to scream, but don't…","text":"Wretched bones and tired look Upon the beaten face Torn flesh that stubbornly Keeps old rags in place Varied shades of grey Cast upon unblinking brow Sullen, sunken eyes Wish to scream, but don't know how Achromatic form, Broken, thrown away Highlighted by red glimmering Among the shades of grey The red, a sign of life A sign the form is still alive A sign that points to willingness A sign of its will to survive"},{"order":94,"slug":"letter","title":"Open Letter","excerpt":"To anyone who reads this To anyone who cares To those who may not realize To those who are aware To those that look away To them that choose to see I'm SCREAMING, CRYING desperately For someone t…","text":"To anyone who reads this To anyone who cares To those who may not realize To those who are aware To those that look away To them that choose to see I'm SCREAMING, CRYING desperately For someone to help me."},{"order":95,"slug":"myplace","title":"My Place","excerpt":"I say I can't deal with it anymore But the very fact that I'm able to say that shows that I have somehow found a way through thus far That I do, in fact, possess the resolve somewhere Whether dee…","text":"I say I can't deal with it anymore But the very fact that I'm able to say that shows that I have somehow found a way through thus far That I do, in fact, possess the resolve somewhere Whether deep inside me Hidden, or freely available And from this well I can draw the strength to carry on Day by day Struggle by struggle Pressing ever on into the great unknown before me Hopeful that one day Peace will beckon me to her sweet embrace And I shall find my place Wrapped in the warm silence of a content soul"},{"order":96,"slug":"embrace","title":"Embracing Change","excerpt":"Impatiently we wait, far beneath the rain clouds Crying out for water, yearning for relief A gentle shower to tide us over Till the heavens decide to inundate us with blessing To reveal their mig…","text":"Impatiently we wait, far beneath the rain clouds Crying out for water, yearning for relief A gentle shower to tide us over Till the heavens decide to inundate us with blessing To reveal their mighty power To demonstrate what we can be What we were meant to be What, deep within, we are And some day, shall be again Let go. Embrace the change. Become."},{"order":97,"slug":"maternal","title":"Maternal Asphyxiation","excerpt":"Gasping for breath, for truth, to be free Struggling to break your hold over me Your hands on my throat is not love, it's not fair Guess I'm dumb, after all my brain's not getting air I know in y…","text":"Gasping for breath, for truth, to be free Struggling to break your hold over me Your hands on my throat is not love, it's not fair Guess I'm dumb, after all my brain's not getting air I know in your mind air is evil, no good I can't see, I don't listen, but you think that I should But my neck has grown, no longer your hands fit my throat I'm telling you now, that it's time to let go"},{"order":98,"slug":"pointfive","title":"0.5","excerpt":"I can’t smile, sing, or laugh, Or be happy, when I am half I must ponder, my sweetest friend, When shall we be one again? For when I am but oh point five, Barely do I feel alive And when I am one…","text":"I can’t smile, sing, or laugh, Or be happy, when I am half I must ponder, my sweetest friend, When shall we be one again? For when I am but oh point five, Barely do I feel alive And when I am one over two, I cannot stand not having you So take the distance that lies between Average it out, and find the mean Divide by five, then times by pi Discover where our midpoint lies And shrink the angle, rise over run Add up the parts, to find the sum Fifty percent, alone’s no fun Add your fifty, we shall be one."},{"order":99,"slug":"abrogation","title":"Abrogation","excerpt":"***Note: Fiction*** If I could, I would choose life for two Life for her, yes, and even life for you As much as you like life, she’d probably like it too But, that choice is not right for you You…","text":"***Note: Fiction*** If I could, I would choose life for two Life for her, yes, and even life for you As much as you like life, she’d probably like it too But, that choice is not right for you You think it’d be easier to divide by two Minus one, and end the life inside of you Even though you do have the right to choose I don’t think that it’s right to do If someone, was trying to take your life from you Wouldn’t you want someone to try to fight for you? And doesn’t she have the same right to life as you? Is it fair, to decide she has her life to lose? But if it won’t make you lose any sleep at night to do And if it’s really what you think you’d like to do I’ll hold your hand, kiss you, and stand right by you Till the rain clouds part, and let the light shine through"},{"order":100,"slug":"whitelies","title":"White Lies","excerpt":"I close my eyes, so I can’t see Then open, still in front of me What is it that you want from me? All that you need, I want to be You hide behind your thin white curtain But you can’t bring yours…","text":"I close my eyes, so I can’t see Then open, still in front of me What is it that you want from me? All that you need, I want to be You hide behind your thin white curtain But you can’t bring yourself to burden The one who’s there to help your health And so you turn to something else Is this about you, or this about me? Looking out from within, or in to see? I search myself only to find feelings mixed It seems our positions have finally switched I can white out the pictures from out of the frames Cover, but under they still remain Turn away, act as though I do not care But because I don’t see, doesn’t mean it’s not there And even though I feign I’m blind I find, inside, I cannot hide Or cover up, or close my eyes Or keep a straight face through my lies And even though you write me off I’m here to help you, if you fall Here to open eyes, help you see That I am here for when you need"},{"order":101,"slug":"glass","title":"Glass Onion","excerpt":"I speak my words through onion breath There's more to what I say To see beyond the surface You must peel the layers away On the outside it looks ugly But dig through deeper down Have an open mind…","text":"I speak my words through onion breath There's more to what I say To see beyond the surface You must peel the layers away On the outside it looks ugly But dig through deeper down Have an open mind Persevere till beauty's found I cannot find the value in Finding something ugly It seems more easy in my mind To find everything lovely Instead of traveling through life With views so dark and hateful For every moment we are here We should be ever greatful And though we walk through fiery trials Instead of merely screaming We should find the good and light in pain Embrace and cling to meaning"},{"order":102,"slug":"behindback","title":"Behind Your Back","excerpt":"I wanna scar my face for all to see The way I feel's your fault to me Why can't you just talk to me? 'Cause being strong's so hard to be Now all I once thought that I knew Has turned out fake, ha…","text":"I wanna scar my face for all to see The way I feel's your fault to me Why can't you just talk to me? 'Cause being strong's so hard to be Now all I once thought that I knew Has turned out fake, havn't you? And if you knew, you'd panic too Seems I can't have truth and have you too I find myself inside your trap How could I be so blind as that? I shed these tears behind your back The good times, can't we rewind to that? I guess since time just flows one way To try is futile, or so some say I'm torn between to go and stay And which is right? I'll know one day."},{"order":103,"slug":"poem","title":"Poem","excerpt":"This my friends, it is a poem And if you need I can go slow I know how sleepy you all are Cause I am too, all day so far So sing a song and dance and laugh Enjoy your hobbies and your crafts But…","text":"This my friends, it is a poem And if you need I can go slow I know how sleepy you all are Cause I am too, all day so far So sing a song and dance and laugh Enjoy your hobbies and your crafts But as for me and my sweet home We'll rock this party all night long"},{"order":104,"slug":"everytime","title":"Every Time","excerpt":"Every time I've held it tight It all has come unwound But every time I've let it go My hands have become bound And every time I've given in I've just let myself down But every time I let it go I…","text":"Every time I've held it tight It all has come unwound But every time I've let it go My hands have become bound And every time I've given in I've just let myself down But every time I let it go I see my strength's been found"},{"order":105,"slug":"allalong","title":"All Along","excerpt":"For the longest time, it seems All I wanted was dreams All of the things that I said Were simply thoughts in my head No matter how hard I would try I simply could not deny My mind's chance to ins…","text":"For the longest time, it seems All I wanted was dreams All of the things that I said Were simply thoughts in my head No matter how hard I would try I simply could not deny My mind's chance to instill That my dreams were not real But one day, as a joke My mind simply awoke And opened up my eyes And made me realize That all I ever wanted That all I'll ever need That all I ever wished for That all that I can see That everything I am That everything that's me Is all I've ever wished for All I've strived so long to be And it might be just beginning Or have been for far too long I may be almost there Or I may be too far gone And maybe I'm correct Or maybe I am wrong But either way, I see today, I've been this all along"},{"order":106,"slug":"together","title":"Together","excerpt":"Everything's mechanical these days But no one seems to notice Even the trees rise above us Like some kind of clouds That are perhaps running Towards the sky Or entrapping the ground all around yo…","text":"Everything's mechanical these days But no one seems to notice Even the trees rise above us Like some kind of clouds That are perhaps running Towards the sky Or entrapping the ground all around you But we never know Until it comes to consume us all Everything is liquid Everything is liquid in this world around me King of ghosts, Spinnning and spreading spiderwebs behind me Who are you that I see in my dreams? What is this face pressed against mine? We're all liquid Melting and blending all together Perfect, just together"}];
